 "stem": "The numbers ${=a}$, ${=b}$ and $c$ are in continued proportion. Find the value of $c$.",
 "answer": "c",
 "solution": [
  "Since $a$, $b$, $c$ are in continued proportion, $b^2=ac$.",
  "${=b}^2={=a}\\times c$, so ${=b*b}={=a}\\,c$.",
  "$c=\\frac{{=b*b}}{{=a}}={=c}$"
 ],
 "proposed_misconceptions": [],
 "notes": "Ratio p/q in lowest terms so c is a whole number."
